# Licensing & Attribution — The Wizard's Castle (MSX2+ Enhanced Port)

This repository combines original MSX2+ game code and documentation with third-party open-source libraries, public-domain reference code, and open-licensed graphical assets.

---

## 1. Combined Work & Repository License (CC BY-SA 4.0)

As a combined work linking against and distributing **MSXgl**, this repository and its compiled binary distributions (`WIZCASTLE.COM`, `WIZDATA.DAT`, and `.DSK` images) are licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0)**.

Additionally, the original C source code and documentation written specifically for the MSX2+ port (located in `MSXgl/projects/wizcastle/` and `docs/`) are dual-licensed under the **MIT License** and **CC BY-SA 4.0**, allowing you to reuse the game's C source code on its own under either license.

---

## 2. Third-Party Credits & Component Licenses

### A. Original Game Concept (1980)
- **Title:** *The Wizard's Castle*
- **Author:** Joseph R. Power
- **Publication:** *Recreational Computing* Magazine (July/August 1980, Vol. 9, No. 1)

### B. WinWiz C++ Port (`winwiz/`) — CC0 1.0 Universal (Public Domain)
- **Author:** Daniel D. Miller
- **License:** [CC0 1.0 Universal (Public Domain Dedication)](winwiz/LICENSE.txt)
- **Summary:** The author dedicated the WinWiz C++ source code to the public domain worldwide, waiving all copyright and related rights.

### C. MSXgl Library (`MSXgl/`) — CC BY-SA 4.0
- **Author:** Guillaume "Aoineko" Blanchard (2022–2025)
- **License:** [Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)](MSXgl/LICENSE.md)
- **Project URL:** https://github.com/aoineko-fr/MSXgl

### D. Graphical Sprites (`winwiz/tiles32.png`) — NetHack General Public License
- **Authors:** M. Stephenson & the NetHack DevTeam
- **License:** NetHack General Public License (permissive open-source license derived from the Bison license; redistribution and modification are permitted provided copyright notices are retained).

